{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Believe and The Sickness feel like natural next choices after Ten Thousand Fists because I want to explore more of Disturbed's mix of aggression and melody.",
    "Mer De Noms connects strongly with my recent interest in 10.000 Days through its atmosphere and Maynard's vocals, while Iowa and City of Evil connect with the heavier side of my listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Fallen feels less suited to what I want now because I am looking for heavier, riff-focused music.",
    "St. Anger's heaviness alone does not make it appealing: its raw, repetitive approach offers less of the melody or atmosphere drawing me to my strongest choices."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat heavy music as broadly interchangeable, although the balance of riffs, melody and atmosphere matters to me.",
    "Godsmack, Hybrid Theory and Death Magnetic share parts of my taste, but that broad resemblance does not give me as strong a reason to choose them today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest listening gives me specific reasons to explore more Disturbed and music connected to Maynard's vocals.",
    "I can want both aggressive metal and atmospheric rock; what matters is how each album develops those qualities, rather than heaviness by itself."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in heavy music, but my strongest choices depend on melody, atmosphere and connections to my latest listening."
}"}
